        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-24T22:28:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "not just that. 1.16 didn\u0027t define I2c, but later revisions did. so, for example, register addresses are wrong.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b3cdf3514853a425cf6df7af3aebbc555c5cfa9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "084381f6_b5d8293b",
        "filename": "docs/cr50_bringup.md",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-25T00:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Frankly, I don\u0027t think this is relevant - the 1.2 spec already defined I2C interface, it is not something  which came along after SPI.",
      "parentUuid": "dc3ae40e_ef4211ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b3cdf3514853a425cf6df7af3aebbc555c5cfa9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e664cd1e_810dd8ed",
        "filename": "docs/cr50_bringup.md",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-25T17:09:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PC Client Profile TPM Profile (PTP) Specification for TPM2.0 level 00 rev 0.43 had only SPI and LPC defined as h/w interfaces.\nThe current one (PC Client Platform TPM Profile Specification for TPM 2.0, version 1.04, revision 37) does have I2C covered. And it has different addresses for TPM registers on I2C compared to SPI/LPC, see section 8.3.5 I2C-TPM Registers. So, our implementation of I2C interface is not compliant with PTP.\n\nIn any case, it may not be very interesting for the intended audience of this doc. The solution here seems to be simple ;)\n\nChange\n\"Both I2C and SPI interfaces do not fully comply with the standards: the I2C\"\nto\n\"Both I2C and SPI interfaces do not fully comply with the standards: for example, the I2C\"",
      "parentUuid": "084381f6_b5d8293b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b3cdf3514853a425cf6df7af3aebbc555c5cfa9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95d91d55_bd99cafb",
        "filename": "docs/cr50_bringup.md",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-25T17:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sentence is not about the TCG standards, it is about I2C and SPI standards, the reader is not expected to be familiar with the TCG platform profile, but is expected to have a working knowledge of SPI and I2C.\n\nI am not sure how to express this better.",
      "parentUuid": "e664cd1e_810dd8ed",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b3cdf3514853a425cf6df7af3aebbc555c5cfa9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cca8ac26_cd3f8bca",
        "filename": "docs/cr50_bringup.md",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
